   "html_text": "Semantic inheritance networks differ from Pollock’s system in two important ways. First, they cannot represent one fact’s constituting an undercutting defeater of an inference, although they can represent rebutting defeaters. For example, they do not allow an inference from the apparent color of an elephant to its actual color to be undercut by the information that my color vision is unreliable, unless I have information about the actual color of the elephant that contradicts its apparent color.",
